[observation.3.7.4]
task = "3.7"
file = "platform/hosted/dashboard/web/url-pattern-globals.d.ts"
symbol = "URLPatternInput URLPatternOptions"
observed = "Observation 3.7.1 blocked the 3.7 verify_cmd at the layerx-dashboard-web image build: tsc --noEmit under the dashboard tsconfig (skipLibCheck false) fails with four errors in next/dist/server/web/spec-extension/url-pattern.d.ts (Cannot find name URLPatternInput / URLPatternOptions). Reproduced on main c7d5e163 with the human web node_modules (next 16.3.1, @types/node 26.2.0, typescript 5.9.3). Root cause: @types/node 26.2.0 web-globals/url.d.ts declares the globals URLPattern, URLPatternInit and URLPatternResult but not URLPatternInput and URLPatternOptions, which node:url does export and which the Next declaration references as globals. The orchestrator repaired it under owner authorization by adding platform/hosted/dashboard/web/url-pattern-globals.d.ts, an ambient declaration binding the two missing global names to the real node:url types; skipLibCheck, the Dockerfile test-then-build step and every other check are unchanged. After the fix tsc --noEmit exits 0 and node tests/ui-contract.mjs exits 0 on main."
assumption = "The missing globals are a typings gap between @types/node 26.2.0 and next 16.3.1 that the developer dashboard owns; binding them to node:url is the faithful repair rather than a weakening. The 3.7 verify_cmd is rerun in main after this change lands."
