observed = "Enumeration of every layerx-internal Service the developer plane dials, from platform/hosted/webhooks/src and platform/hosted/dashboard/src. redis.layerx-internal.svc:6379 (rediss, TLS 1.2+, no client certificate, AUTH username password per connection): webhooks RedisRepository uses PING, HMGET webhooks:principal:<sha256 principal> revision json, EVAL of a CAS script touching webhooks:principal:* and webhooks:principals (needs +@scripting), SMEMBERS webhooks:principals and HGET; dashboard gateway::Store reads only PING, SMEMBERS gateway:principal:<digest>:keys, HMGET gateway:key:<id>, GET gateway:quota:<id>:<window> and XREVRANGE gateway:audit, so the dashboard's view is the gateway's own key space. kms.layerx-internal.svc:443 (HTTPS, mTLS developer-client identity plus bearer): POST /v1/signing-keys with Idempotency-Key and body {algorithm:ed25519,purpose:layerx-webhook-v1} answering 200 or 201 {key_id,handle,public_key} (deny_unknown_fields, key_id whk_-prefixed and at most 64 identifier bytes, handle at most 512 bytes, public_key padded base64 of 32 bytes), POST /v1/signatures {key_handle,algorithm,message} answering {signature} of 64 base64 bytes verified locally against the recorded public key, GET /readyz answering exactly {ready,ed25519_non_exportable} with both true. identity.layerx-internal.svc:443: POST /v1/sessions/introspect {token} answering {active,sub,csrf_token} for the webhooks and dashboard service tokens, not part of readiness. component.layerx-internal.svc:443: GET /readyz 200 and GET /internal/v1/receipts/{activity_id} answering {activity_id,receipt}. authority.layerx-internal.svc:443: GET /readyz 200 and GET /internal/v1/activities/{activity_id}/authority answering the eight-field authority body cross-checked against LAYERX_WEBHOOKS_NETWORK_ID, LAYERX_WEBHOOKS_LXP_WIRE_VERSION and the sequencer public key. journeys, payments, approvals and programs .layerx-internal.svc:443: GET /readyz 200 and GET /internal/v1/events/{id} answering {id,principal,subject,subject_sequence,occurred_at,facts:[{name,value}],activity_id?,amount?,asset?} with deny_unknown_fields, at most 32 facts, id equal to the requested id, payment requiring activity_id, digit amount and asset. Readiness: webhooks /healthz is Redis PING and KMS /readyz and component, authority and all four source /readyz; dashboard /healthz is the two Redis PINGs. The TLS verification name is the literal env host, so every alias target must present a certificate carrying its layerx-internal.svc name. The hosted identity, receipt authority and agent boundary of tasks 6.3 to 6.5 already serve the routes above on port 9443; the developer plane dials port 443. No KMS server, no layerx-internal namespace, no Redis ACL for the two developer users and no event-source producer exist in the repository, and the human service that journeys and approvals are specified to be backed by is not part of the beta cluster bring-up."
