[observation.6.4.4]
task = "6.4"
file = "platform/hosted/agent-boundary/tests/real_node.rs"
symbol = "signed_program_call real_program_call_refusal_artifacts_are_bound_and_replay_after_restart"
observed = "The task verify_cmd's cargo test -p layerx-platform-agent-boundary against the rebuilt build/bin binaries fails 3 of 4 real-node tests (/tmp/layerx-64-boundary-test.log, exit 101) and its strict clippy fails on too_many_lines at tests/real_node.rs:1639 and src/main.rs:1055 (/tmp/layerx-64-boundary-clippy.log, exit 101); both files are uncommitted work of the boundary lane. Two failures are test-harness: real_node_boundary_serves_the_component_contract dies with exit 126 Text file busy when a parallel test copies the boundary binary that another test is executing, and real_program_simulation_executes_without_committing expects 503 where the boundary answers 409 module_disabled. The third is a genuine cross-lane contradiction with native evidence: signed_program_call encodes layerx_types::intent::ProgramCall::canonical_payload (domain, callee, fuel, fee limit, capability count, calldata), while src/modules/programs/call.c lxp_programs_call_decode requires the 106-byte fixed layout (program id, abi version, entrypoint length, calldata length, capabilities length, access declaration length, response capacity, seven budget fields) and returns LXP_ERR_TRUNCATED on the shorter payload. Because cmd/layerxd/lxp_daemon_lni.c admits any LX_PROGRAMS_CALL envelope without decoding its payload and cmd/layerxd/lxp_daemon_process.c apply_canonical_batch treats a schedule-item decode failure as a batch failure, the daemon logs execution failed at sequence 1 with result -1, stops accepting, and the boundary answers 202 unknown forever; the test then fails asserting 200."
assumption = "The daemon halting on a signed but non-canonical ProgramCall payload from an authenticated boundary is a native admission gap: the payload should be refused at LNI admission or answered with a typed refusal receipt rather than poisoning the sequencer. It is outside the protocol-3 execution repair and is left intact for the native owner; the boundary test builder must produce the daemon's canonical ProgramCall payload before the verify_cmd can pass. Task 6.4 stays in_progress."
severity = "blocker"

