observed = "Two independent scalar failures are repaired. Protocol-3 SEND admission now rejects an already-unpayable signed fee limit before durable queue admission, preserving known replay handling and the kernel fee policy. Enqueue and recovered-queue restoration now broadcast queue_changed because the executor and auxiliary workers share the condition; signaling one waiter could wake an auxiliary worker and strand the executor with acknowledged work. The real multiworker core regression proves fee 1000 from an empty account returns HTTP 422 and exact LNI class 4/result -602, leaves the chain head unchanged and remains ready; a fee-zero request using the same account sequence then produces the original verified signed terminal refusal receipt. The full core, authority and agent-boundary test command passes: 5 core boundary tests, 1 native SEND test, 2 authority real-node tests, 5 agent-boundary real-node tests and 1 artifact unit test. Strict all-target clippy for all three packages passes. Logs /tmp/layerx-core-queue-wake-all-test.log and /tmp/layerx-core-queue-wake-clippy.log. Native daemon and durable admission gates also pass: make --no-print-directory -s -j2 test-layerxd test-daemon-lni-admission, /tmp/layerx-native-queue-wake-daemon-tests.log, exit 0. Production daemon a328570021e0754dc79a4c5055da02fb04a7da6fb7e709fc789b49ca1d4a49b3 contains no temporary stage diagnostics."
assumption = "This supersedes observation 6.2.4 for the scalar receipt failure. A genuine first refused batch can now bootstrap checkpoint production without funded execution, but the live guarantor batch producer, finalized-custody deposit-root publisher and native issuance activity remain absent. Admission checks current balance, not reservations against all future queued spends. Treasury funding and full beta readiness are not qualified by these passing refusal and lifecycle gates."
severity = "note"

