observed = "Lines 146, 158 and 170 supply zero r and s and malformed zero SEC1 keys; runtime reports MalformedSignature instead of expected VerificationFailed. Line 219 supplies zero r and s for recovery ids 0..3; runtime reports MalformedSignature instead of RecoveryFailed. ECDSA requires nonzero r and s, although libsecp256k1 compact parsing permits zero encodings and rejects them at verification. Line 266 supplies an alleged published ECDSA vector that OpenSSL also rejects for the supplied digest; its provenance is unestablished. Line 301 uses Ed25519 public key [02;32], whose derived x-squared is a quadratic nonresidue under RFC 8032 point decoding, and an S outside the RFC bound; runtime reports MalformedPublicKey instead of VerificationFailed. Line 315 has r=0 and s=255, not a high-S signature, and runtime reports MalformedSignature instead of VerificationFailed. Existing invalid recovery-id cases 4 and 255 agree with the libsecp256k1 range. No original expectation is changed."
assumption = "The runtime-defect stop interrupts the seven-case reconciliation. Independent rejection alone does not establish the exact LayerX refusal enum. No genuine high-S coverage or original-vector provenance is claimed. Raw evidence: qual-logs/signatures/reference-check.log and targets.log; exact runtime defect inputs and owner request are in untracked NEEDS.md."
