[observation.6.6.comet_genesis_boundary]
task = "6.6"
file = "platform/hosted/paxeer/src/genesis.rs"
symbol = "endpoint fetch chunked_genesis response"
observed = "GET /genesis is enabled only by LAYERX_PAXEER_COMET_URL, a literal loopback HTTP origin. It extracts the exact genesis JSON bytes from the configured Comet response and returns X-LayerX-Genesis-SHA256 over those bytes. The HTTP GET response shapes in paxeer-network/consensus/rpc/jsonrpc/server/http_server.go are bare results or errors; standard JSON-RPC envelopes are also parsed explicitly. Only the exact internal-error code, message and genesis_chunked data text permit ordered chunk retrieval. Counts, indices, base64 padding, JSON, chain_id, a separate 32 MiB genesis limit, 32-chunk cap and aggregate 30-second upstream timeout are checked. Existing EVM body bounds and method restrictions are unchanged. The primary boundary manifest configures http://127.0.0.1:26657. Tests execute the actual TLS binary against a loopback HTTP listener serving a byte-identical copy of paxeer-network/node/genesis/chains/pacific-1.json, including framing, exact-byte hashing, ordered reassembly, malformed input, size limits, timeout, unavailable upstream and unset-variable 404 cases. No new dependency or lockfile entry is introduced; serde_json raw_value preserves the returned representation and the existing rustls provider supplies SHA256."
assumption = "Full cargo test and platform-test-paxeer-boundary invoke tests/real_chain.py, which initializes and transacts on chain 125; the current isolation constraint prohibits those transactions. Focused genesis qualification does not establish the full real-chain gate or hosted deployment. The observer boundary must explicitly configure its own Comet origin http://127.0.0.1:26667, and identity evidence consumers must hash the exact response body before binding its chain_id to the EVM chain identity."
severity = "note"

[observation.6.6.disposable_comet_genesis]
task = "6.6"
file = "platform/hosted/paxeer/tests/real_chain.py"
symbol = "real_paxd_boundary raw_request"
observed = "The disposable test configures LAYERX_PAXEER_COMET_URL from its ephemeral LAYERX_PAXEER_RPC_PORT and exercises GET /genesis through the real TLS boundary against a source-built paxd. It checks the single X-LayerX-Genesis-SHA256 header against exact response bytes, binds hyperpax_125-1 to eth_chainId 125, and compares the entire document with the initialized genesis in Comet wire representation. The initial full run and diagnostic run exited 101 because the on-disk ABCI vote_extensions_enable_height is an integer while consensus/libs/json/encoder.go emits int64 as a decimal string. Expected-document construction now explicitly projects that field to its required wire representation; full-document equality and every existing assertion remain enforced. Logs: qual-logs/second-cargo-test.log and qual-logs/second-genesis-diagnostic.log. make -C paxeer-network build exits 0 in qual-logs/second-paxd-build.log with GOFLAGS=-p=4. Full cargo test --locked --manifest-path platform/Cargo.toml -p layerx-platform-paxeer-boundary exits 0 in qual-logs/second-cargo-test-fixed.log. make platform-test-paxeer-boundary exits 0 in qual-logs/second-make-test.log. Package format check and strict all-target Clippy exit 0 in qual-logs/second-fmt.log and qual-logs/second-clippy.log. CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=4 and MAKEFLAGS=-j4 apply."
assumption = "The earlier disposable-chain authorization blocker is resolved. The script uses a temporary home and ephemeral loopback listeners, with no persistent-chain port, fixed home or systemd access. These gates establish local disposable runtime coverage, not hosted deployment. The observer boundary still needs its own Comet origin configured and identity consumers must verify exact-body hashing and bind Comet and EVM identities."
severity = "note"

